WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.869
-The president and GOP leaders
are insisting

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:05.972
that Trump's latest
racist comments are not,

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.140
in fact, racist,
despite the fact that

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.176
they are definitely
super racist.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.377
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:13.079
For more on this, it's time for
"A Closer Look."

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.415
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:21.253
Trump has spent the week reeling
off a series of unhinged tweets

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:23.323
and tirades
defending his racist attack

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:25.458
on four Democratic
congresswomen of color,

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.860
in which he told them to go back
and help fix

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.062
the "totally broken
and crime-infested places"

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.130
from which they came.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.798
Of course,
they're Americans.

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:34.133
Three of them
were born here,

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.602
and the fourth is a refugee
and naturalized citizen.

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:39.005
So, if their country
is broken and crime-infested,

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.306
that's on you.

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:42.642
Trump accidentally...

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.944
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:48.447
Trump accidentally
burned himself.

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:50.950
It's like if someone said,
"Man, your parents

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.452
must have really
screwed you up,"

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.487
and that someone
was your mom.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.955
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.826
So, given the fact that
they're American citizens,

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:02.061
reporters this afternoon
followed up on Trump's comments,

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.530
and he once again
defended them.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.732
-If people want to leave
our country, they can.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.266
If they don't want to
love our country,

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:08.668
if they don't want to
fight for our country,

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:09.902
they can.

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.304
I'll never change on that.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:14.507
They are not espousing
the views of our country,

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.243
the four congresswomen.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.278
I think that
they've said horrible things

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:20.646
that the press
doesn't cover.

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:22.415
I think you should try
covering it.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.483
When you look at some of
the things they said,

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:25.985
they're unthinkable.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.421
If somebody else, or --
me, or anybody else --

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:32.792
said things like that,
it would be historic.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.094
So, you ought to look at some of
their horrible statements,

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.363
'cause there's never been
statements like that.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.333
-Trump's brain disease
won't let him backtrack,

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.768
no matter how far over the line
he goes.

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:44.537
If he said,
"I'm gonna eat this apple,"

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.272
and you said,
"Dude, that's an onion,"

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.941
he would stand there
and eat the whole thing

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:51.244
with tears
streaming down his face.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.378
[ As Trump ]
"This is a really--

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.947
this is a
really good apple.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.381
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.382
"Is this a
golden delicious?"

00:01:57.382 --> 00:01:59.152
[Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:04.590
[ Normal voice ]
Also, those congresswomen
do love our country,

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.525
as evidenced by the fact
that they've chosen

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:08.694
to spend their time and energy
serving in Congress

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:11.230
despite having to deal with
your bull[bleep] every day.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.398
I mean, if I...

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:15.401
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.603
If I had to do their jobs
for one day,

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:20.139
I'd be like, "[Bleep] it.
I'm moving to Maine."

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:21.473
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.473 --> 00:02:23.042
"I'm gonna open up one of
those trendy furniture stores

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.945
that sells tree stump
coffee tables."

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.480
I mean, all I do
is make fun of you,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.681
and I'm exhausted.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.082
This is what I looked like

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:32.018
when the Trump
administration started.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.486
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.221
I mean, who needs --

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:38.458
Who needs FaceApp when you have
Trump for a president?

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.726
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.461
Also, you're accusing them
of saying horrible things

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.762
about our country?

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.497
You spent the eight years
of the Obama administration

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.866
and the 2016 campaign
constantly lying

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.601
and trash-talking
the country.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:54.240
-The U.S. has become
a dumping ground

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.242
for everybody
else's problems.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.110
We're like a dumping ground
for the world.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.312
We're a dumping ground.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.580
The United States
is becoming a dumping ground.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.716
We used to be at the top.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.685
Now, we're like
a third-world country.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.287
We're like
a third-world country.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:09.488
We're becoming
a third-world country

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:11.090
because of our
infrastructure --

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.259
our airports, our roads,
everything.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.896
The whole world is looking at
us, and laughing at us.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.630
The world is
laughing at us.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.367
They're laughing at the
stupidity of our president.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.935
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.904
Well...

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.073
Well, I'm glad that's over.

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:31.510
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.479
So, Trump called America
a "dumping ground,"

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.381
a "third-world country,"
and a "laughingstock."

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.783
I'd tell him to go back to
where he came from,

00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:39.685
but I'm pretty sure
he just appeared

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:41.754
after a bunch of teens
played with a ouija board

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.689
they found in the woods.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.258
Of course,
since it summoned Trump,

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.593
the word "ouija"
was probably misspelled.

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:49.728
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.728 --> 00:03:51.364
So, Trump mounted
a racist attack

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.032
on four Democratic
congresswomen of color,

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.600
and then defended that attack
with lies

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.902
about the congresswomen
he was attacking --

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.203
which, of course,
gave Republicans a chance

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.172
to courageously stand up
to the president

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.873
by pulling
their favorite move --

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.675
pretending they haven't
heard about it,

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:06.045
and desperately waiting for
the elevator doors to close.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.213
Here's one senator

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.715
trying out an especially
unconvincing response.

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:11.750
-You saw the president's tweets
this weekend.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.786
-Actually,
I was out of town.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:14.887
-Oh!

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.055
Well, actually --

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.857
Actually, twitter has
a new feature

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.659
where you can even read
the tweets out of town.

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:21.694
[Laughter]

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.397
The way it works is
the [bleep] same.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:25.397
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:27.032
Anyway, go on.

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:29.868
-Well, he said that
these progressive congresswomen

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:32.738
should go back
to their countries.

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:36.075
I'm wondering what your reaction
is to that.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:41.614
-I'm working hard as I can
on reducing healthcare costs.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.482
I'm not giving
a daily commentary

00:04:43.482 --> 00:04:44.550
of the president's tweets.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.620
-But these are, you know,
racist tweets.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.922
Do you have any concerns
about it?

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:55.495
-The president said that
these minority congresswomen

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.595
should go back to
their countries.

00:04:56.595 --> 00:04:57.797
Do you have a response?

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.566
-I haven't read that,
but I'll go check it out.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:01.768
-Okay.

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:04.170
-Man, what would Republicans
in Congress do

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.139
if the Capitol
didn't have elevators?

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:07.573
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.775
They'd have to
carry around houseplants

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:11.811
just so they could
hide behind them.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.246
"What do you think of
the president's tweets?"

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.547
"I'm sorry,
I haven't seen them.

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:18.384
Now, if you'll
excuse me, I..."

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.853
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:05:31.363 --> 00:05:32.865
"Is he gone?"

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.669
Also, I'm sorry,
but can we please retire this

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:37.970
"I haven't seen
the tweet" excuse?

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.104
No one believes you.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:40.640
In fact, this excuse
is getting so absurd

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.942
that Trump's acting director
of U.S. Citizenship

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.710
and Immigration Services,
Ken Cuccinelli,

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:48.046
tried it on CNN
literally right after an anchor

00:05:48.046 --> 00:05:49.515
read the tweet on air.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.750
-The president sent this out
yesterday at 8:00 a.m.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.053
"So interesting to see
progressive Democratic

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.622
congresswomen who originally
came from countries

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:59.358
whose governments are a complete
and total catastrophe --

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:02.728
the worst, most corrupt, and
inept anywhere in the world --

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:05.130
if they even have a functioning
government at all --

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.668
now loudly and viciously telling
the people of the United States,

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.770
the greatest and most powerful
nation on Earth,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.805
how our government
is to be run.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:16.141
Why don't they go back and help
fix the totally broken

00:06:16.141 --> 00:06:20.079
and crime-infested places
from which they came?"

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.114
What did you think
of that tweet?

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:25.151
-Well, I didn't see
that tweet, actually.

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.785
I can hear what
you're reading.

00:06:26.785 --> 00:06:29.288
-Yeah, you ca--
You just heard it.

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:30.656
She just read it to you.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.391
Republicans are like
your friends

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:35.327
who haven't seen a TV show
trying to avoid spoilers

00:06:35.327 --> 00:06:37.730
while they're watching
the show.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.065
"No, no, no.
Don't give it away!"

00:06:40.065 --> 00:06:42.567
Seriously, the only way you can
support Trump without lying,

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.737
at this point, is if you have
the part of your brain

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:46.138
that's responsible
for memory

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:48.807
replaced with the brain
of a goldfish.

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:49.941
"I hadn't seen the tweet."

00:06:49.941 --> 00:06:51.043
"I just showed you
the tweet."

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.612
"What tweet?"
"The president's tweet."

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:55.414
"Sorry, one sec.
I got eat these food flakes."

00:06:55.414 --> 00:07:00.519
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:03.689
By the way,
just to give you an idea

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.090
of how fully and completely

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.359
Republicans have debased
themselves in service of Trump,

00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:09.195
that same guy,
Ken Cuccinelli,

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:12.264
staged a floor fight at the 2016
Republican National Convention

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:14.767
to change the convention rules,
and even made a big show

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.735
of dramatically throwing
his credentials on the floor.

00:07:16.735 --> 00:07:19.605
And after that happened,
Trump's son, Donald Trump Jr.,

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.907
slammed Cuccinelli,
and called him an "idiot."

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:24.143
-I have the same group of
four people running around.

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:25.344
They wait for a camera
to show up,

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.512
and then, they take
their credentials,

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:28.346
and tried to dramatically
throw them on the floor.

00:07:28.346 --> 00:07:29.515
They look like idiots.

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:30.516
-You're talking about
Ken Cuccinelli.

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:31.751
Are you calling him
an idiot?

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:33.085
I'm saying these people
look like idiots

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:34.820
when they're doing that.
-Imagine --

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.655
Imagine how pathetic
you have to be

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:38.257
to take a job in
the Trump administration

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:41.160
after Donald Trump Jr.
called you an idiot.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.361
Donald Trump Jr.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:44.230
This is a guy who doesn't even
know how to stand

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.331
like a normal
human being.

00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:47.466
I mean, look at him.

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:49.001
He always looks like
he's waiting for someone

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:51.670
to pin a medal
on his chest.

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:54.740
"My father said I was getting
an award for most oily."

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.575
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.575 --> 00:07:59.111
What all this is exposing,
once again,

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:02.181
is the rot of intellectual
bad faith within the GOP.

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:04.083
For years,
they claimed that,

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.052
when they criticized
President Obama,

00:08:06.052 --> 00:08:07.920
they were just
upholding the Constitution,

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.154
and they complained

00:08:09.154 --> 00:08:11.491
they were being unfairly
maligned as racists.

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:13.959
And to prove that
they would be consistent,

00:08:13.959 --> 00:08:16.195
they said they would also stand
up to a Republican president.

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:18.097
For example, according to
a new book out this week,

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:19.932
then-Republican Congressman
Mick Mulvaney,

00:08:19.932 --> 00:08:22.368
who is now Trump's
acting chief of staff,

00:08:22.368 --> 00:08:24.970
said back in 2016,
"We're not going to let Trump

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.405
dismantle the
Bill of Rights.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:27.974
For five and a half years,
every time we got to the floor,

00:08:27.974 --> 00:08:30.109
and tried to push back against
an over-reaching president,

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:34.212
we get accused of being partisan
at best, and racist at worst.

00:08:34.212 --> 00:08:35.847
When we do it against
a Republican president,

00:08:35.847 --> 00:08:38.517
maybe people will see
it was a principled objection

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:39.585
in the first place."

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:41.187
Well, they didn't,
because it wasn't.

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:43.188
Republicans are literally
hiding in elevators

00:08:43.188 --> 00:08:44.890
to avoid
criticizing Trump.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:46.825
If you get in an elevator
with a Republican Senator,

00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:49.128
be careful, because they might
hit every button.

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:50.329
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:51.630
"Sorry, just need
a couple minutes.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.099
Hey, can you show me
how to open Twitter?

00:08:54.099 --> 00:08:55.901
No, no,
not the regular one.

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:57.837
Travel Twitter.

00:08:57.837 --> 00:09:01.039
Oh. Oh, God, man,
it has been a day.

00:09:01.039 --> 00:09:04.376
It has been --
Oh, it has been..."

00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:08.080
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:10.582 --> 00:09:13.419
The last few days have exposed
once again that the eight years

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:14.920
Republicans spent
criticizing Obama

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.856
weren't actually about
principled objections.

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:18.891
The same guys who said
they'd stand up to Trump

00:09:18.891 --> 00:09:20.726
are now working for him,
or hiding in elevators

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:23.429
to avoid criticizing
the racism and corruption and...

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:25.264
-Stupidity of our president.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:26.832
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:30.870
[ Cheers and applause ]

